# Native installation configuration examples.
# Startup does not execute .env. Export the chosen values in the service environment.
# Keep runtime configuration, owner credentials and managed account files outside
# every agent workspace. See docs/architecture/owned-product-runtime.md.

# Existing source database: explicit selection does not move or restore data.
# INFINIBAY_DB=/absolute/path/to/source.db

# Logs and the default attachment root (<INFINIBAY_DATA>/uploads).
# Defaults to .data below the working directory; DB selection remains independent.
# INFINIBAY_DATA=/absolute/path/to/product-data
# Preserve an existing attachment directory explicitly when changing installation.
# INFINIBAY_UPLOAD_BASE_DIR=/absolute/path/to/existing/uploads

# Compiled web assets; defaults to frontend/dist below the working directory.
# INFINIBAY_STATIC_DIR=/absolute/path/to/frontend/dist

# Private user-owned directory outside workspaces, mode 0700.
# INFINIBAY_AUTH_DIR=/absolute/path/to/private-owner-auth

# Native Codex subscription, mandatory published ken-rank MCP, host resources and
# initial model selection are configured in this external JSON. No API-key fallback.
# INFINIBAY_RUNTIME_CONFIG=/absolute/path/to/runtime-owned.json

# Optional documentation provider: separate quota, configured on the host only.
# CONTEXT7_API_KEY=
# Historical INFINIBAY_CONTEXT7_API_KEY is accepted when the new name is empty.

# Optional native web capture: separate provider quota, never copied to agents.
# SPIDER_API_KEY=
# SPIDER_MAX_CREDITS=100
# Historical INFINIBAY_SPIDER_API_KEY is accepted when the new name is empty.

# Forgejo is an independently provisioned service. Existing state needs an upgrade
# rehearsal and a consistent backup; normal Researcher startup does not provision it.
# FORGEJO_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1
# FORGEJO_OWNER=your-forgejo-user
